/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  curate640_vp_methylButanoate -- the vapour pressure of methylButanoate, REFITTED to
  measurements (DEV.md 4c C281 and C283).  Written by `bin/choupo-curate vp
  methylButanoate`; everything above the RESULT paragraph is the DECLARATION,
  committed before any fit ran, so it can be read against the result.

  WHY.  The catalogue record carried `vaporPressure { model AmbroseWalton; }`,
  a corresponding-states ESTIMATE from Tc, Pc and omega that never reads the
  record's own Tb (C279 measured a median 19.6 % AAD over the 25 such records
  with archive data).  Here a three-parameter Antoine is fitted to EVERY
  usable laboratory's measurements of it.

  STUDIES (one per article, extracted by `choupo-thermoml extract-vp`; ranked
  by points, ties by DOI):
      10.1021/je034290l                95 pts  347.53-392.2 K  Ortega; Espiau; Postigo
      10.1021/je300799f                58 pts  354.1-412.83 K  Rios; Ortega; Fernandez
      10.1016/j.fluid.2008.02.001      24 pts  274.3-303.2 K  Verevkin; Emel'yanenko
      10.1016/j.jct.2011.10.001        14 pts  316.24-375.25 K  Agafonova; Varushchenko; Druzhinina; Polyakova
  SET ASIDE BY NAME:
      10.1021/je060469v: 1 pressure point(s), fewer than 5

  FIT AND GRADED ACCEPTANCE (DEV.md 4c C285, Vitor 2026-11-10; the evidence,
  objective and outliers of C283; declared before the fit).
  EVIDENCE: every study above is fitted; none is held out (C283 amended:
  laboratories disagree with each other by more than they claim, so the
  test is agreement across all of them, not one laboratory's claimed
  precision).  OBJECTIVE: `objective { method twoStage; }` -- least
  squares in log10 P for a first estimate, then the LARGEST relative error in
  P, (P_model - P)/P, over the kept points minimised from it (Vitor's
  practice, C280); both answers kept.  OUTLIERS: after the least-squares
  stage a point with a relative P error above 15 % (three times
  the acceptance) is DISCARDED BY NAME (its study DOI, T and P), listed in
  the result and the record, and the fit repeated without it, once
  (`outliers { maxRelativeError 15 percent; }`).  ACCEPTANCE,
  GRADED, the DEFAULT of C285: the maximum relative P error over all kept
  points is graded clean up to 5 %, warning up to
  10 %, severe up to 20 % and refused above; where the
  normal-boiling-point condition below applies, the absolute gap is graded
  clean up to 1 K, warning up to 2 K, severe up to
  4 K and refused above.  The fit's grade is the WORSE of the
  two.  A clean, warning or severe fit is ACCEPTED and promoted (autoPromoted,
  humanReviewed false) with `fitGrade <grade>;` and the deciding numbers in
  its provenance entry, which the component loader voices on every run that
  uses it (a warning or a severe grade); a refused one is not promoted.  This
  case declares no `system/curationDict`, so the default applies; a case
  that needs another acceptance declares it there, with its reason.  The
  AmbroseWalton curve's errors on the same points are reported beside the
  fit's, as information.

  NORMAL BOILING POINT: no Tb declared in the record: no normal-boiling-point condition.

  NO MEASURED POINT IS IN THIS TREE: constant/archiveDatasets declares every
  series by DOI, NIST URL and sha256; `bin/choupo-curate fetch` regenerates
  them into constant/archiveExtracts/ (gitignored).

  RESULT
  @@RESULT-BEGIN@@
  WHAT THE RUN FOUND (pinned in `expected`; measured, not argued).
  Objective twoStage. Antoine log10(Psat/bar) = 4.105306 - 1260.1748/(T +
  -66.9247), in-sample R2 0.999462 over 191 kept points, 274.3-412.83 K
  (10.1021/je034290l 95/95 kept; 10.1021/je300799f 58/58 kept;
  10.1016/j.fluid.2008.02.001 24/24 kept; 10.1016/j.jct.2011.10.001 14/14
  kept). Relative error in P over the kept points: mean 2.9097 %, max
  4.8925 %; AmbroseWalton on the same points: mean 16.9298 %, max 44.3167
  %. Outliers discarded: none. Its own normal boiling point (101.325
  kPa): 374.32 K. PROMOTED (and since REVERTED by `choupo-curate revert`)
  on 2026-11-10 into data/standards/components/methylButanoate.dat as
  reviewStatus autoPromoted, humanReviewed false, because: fit grade
  clean under the DEFAULT graded acceptance of DEV.md 4c C285 (no
  system/curationDict), 4 studies, 191 points kept, 0 discarded as
  outliers; max relative error 4.892 % (mean 2.91 %), grade clean (limits
  5 / 10 / 20 %); no Tb declared; AmbroseWalton on the same points mean
  16.93 % / max 44.32 %
  @@RESULT-END@@
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

operations
(
    {
        name       fit_antoine;
        type       vaporPressureFit;
        component  methylButanoate;

        evidence
        (
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/methylButanoate-vapourPressure-je034290l.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je034290l"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/methylButanoate-vapourPressure-je300799f.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1021/je300799f"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/methylButanoate-vapourPressure-j.fluid.2008.02.001.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1016/j.fluid.2008.02.001"; }
                role      fit;
            }
            {
                dataset   "constant/archiveExtracts/methylButanoate-vapourPressure-j.jct.2011.10.001.dat";
                identity  { doi "10.1016/j.jct.2011.10.001"; }
                role      fit;
            }
        );

        objective  { method twoStage; }
        outliers   { maxRelativeError 15 percent; }

        output     { file fit_antoine.csv; }
    }
);
